{"segments": [
 {"id": "hero-01", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "Iʿrāb in the Qur'an. Ten verses.", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "hero-02", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "These are real verses. Each one has a past verb and a naṣb noun.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["sub"]},
 {"id": "hero-03", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "They also use the rafʿ and jarr rules we already know.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "hero-04", "scene": "hero", "lang": "en", "text": "Same colours. Same method.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-title-01", "scene": "c01-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter one. Three small notes for these verses.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c01-notes-01", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "First note. Attached pronouns are fixed.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:1"]},
 {"id": "c01-notes-02", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "His, her and your can be short endings. They join the noun before them.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-03", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "They are the owner.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-04", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "We split them off, so you can see the noun's ending. Take his Lord.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-05", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "رَبَّهُ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-06", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "His is the small piece at the end.", "pause": 0.6, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-07", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "Second note. A past verb can hide its doer.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:2"]},
 {"id": "c01-notes-08", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "An order verb hides the word you. In the same way, a past verb can hide the word he.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-09", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "(هُوَ)", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-10", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "It can also hide the word she.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-11", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "(هِيَ)", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-12", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "This verb means she tore.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-13", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "قَدَّتْ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-14", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "The ending of this verb tells us the doer is she.", "pause": 0.6, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-15", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "Third note. Some names never take tanween.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["note:3"]},
 {"id": "c01-notes-16", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "آدَمُ", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-17", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "سُلَيْمَانُ", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-18", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "دَاوُودَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-19", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "One damma or one fatha only.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-20", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "en", "text": "But names like Nuh do take tanween.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-notes-21", "scene": "c01-notes", "lang": "ar", "text": "نُوحٌ", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-also-01", "scene": "c01-also", "lang": "en", "text": "Also. Some past verbs end in a letter with sukūn, like the verb in the second note.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["show"]},
 {"id": "c01-also-02", "scene": "c01-also", "lang": "en", "text": "Before al, that last letter takes a small kasra, just like an order verb.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-also-03", "scene": "c01-also", "lang": "en", "text": "She closed the doors.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-also-04", "scene": "c01-also", "lang": "ar", "text": "غَلَّقَتِ الأَبْوَابَ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c01-also-05", "scene": "c01-also", "lang": "en", "text": "It is still fixed.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c02-title-01", "scene": "c02-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter two. The colour key.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-01", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Navy is the verb. Past and order verbs are fixed.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["key:verb"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-02", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Orange is the doer. Who did the action? It takes rafʿ.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["key:doer"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-03", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "The next four jobs all take naṣb.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c02-key-04", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Pink is the object. What? Whom?", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["key:obj"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-05", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Teal is the purpose. Why?", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["key:purp"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-06", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Brown is time or place. When? Where? With no preposition.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["key:when"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-07", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "Olive is the state. How?", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["key:state"]},
 {"id": "c02-key-08", "scene": "c02-key", "lang": "en", "text": "The small boxes from last lesson still work. After a preposition. Ownership. Adjective. And after wa.", "pause": 0.7, "cues": ["old"]},
 {"id": "c03-title-01", "scene": "c03-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter three. The ten verses.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c03-title-02", "scene": "c03-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Read each verse aloud with your teacher first. Then solve the cards. Every ending is missing.", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["sub"]},
 {"id": "c03-overview-01", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "Each row is one verse. Next to it are its reference and the jobs inside it.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["row:1"]},
 {"id": "c03-overview-02", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "Most of them are a short piece of a longer verse.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["rows"]},
 {"id": "c03-overview-03", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "On screen, they are written in our usual spelling.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-overview-04", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "The naṣb noun is an object, a time, or a state.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-overview-05", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "For each verse, we first hear its meaning. Then we hear it recited.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c03-overview-06", "scene": "c03-overview", "lang": "en", "text": "After that, we box it together, piece by piece.", "pause": 0.8, "cues": []}
]}
